      "result_description": "Barking CC - 3rd XI - Won",
      "result_applied_to": "33697",
      "match_notes": "On a dull saturday morning Barking 3rds went up against Rainham 2nds. Barking won the toss and batted first. A brilliant start by Rainham with the ball taking two quick wickets but some good batting by A.Khan making partnerships with W.Khan and L.Vickery in which they both showed promice but fell cheap by giving there wickets away. Barking were setting eyes on there famaous collapses but were helped by some good batting lower down the order with most batsmen getting starts but not carrying on not forgetting a well fought 45 from V.Hinds. Barking ended there innings short of the 45 over mark on 224. Rainham's innings was a lone battle by Callaghan scoring 103 retired not out with a good 9th wicket partnership with youngster R.Simms who showed real promise in his batting abilities making a well fought 17. There wasn't much from others as there were 5 ducks from the rest of the team ending with a total of 150 for 9. Good bowling by Q.Quershi, A.Siddiqui and V.Hinds. Great victory for Bark",
